New telescopes with super-sensitive tools have changed the way we understand active galaxies over the past 20 years. These powerful tools have given us: 

(a) the strongest proof yet that all powerful radio galaxies are connected in a certain way; 
(b) a better understanding of the colors and shapes of the galaxies that host these powerful radio sources, no matter how far away they are; 
(c) important clues about how the light is scattered around these galaxies on a very small scale.
